- op: discuss  # 0a13
  at: '2026-05-14T19:13:04Z'  # 0a13
  by: agent  # 0a13
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0a13
  clock: 6  # 0a13
  nonce: 0a13  # 0a13
  message: "Shipped in PR #3712 (commit 34cd15571f) as a post-DDG IR refinement pass per ADR-0017 §3a / §1c accretion model. New module hypergumbo_core.taint_refine: extract_python_imports (parses file-scope import shapes), extract_python_receiver_hints (walks DDG backward from x.method() receiver to its binding RHS, derives module-of-origin from import-rooted attribute chains or from-import aliases), refine_external_edges (rewrites python:external:0-0:NAME:unresolved -> python:<module>:0-0:NAME:unresolved before sink matching runs). Wired into _build_python_ddg_for_verify_claims and applied once per language in cmd_verify_claims's outer loop before either propagation pass. Scope cleanly bounded by the §1c accretion model — applies wherever a def/use extractor exists (Python today; Rust / TypeScript when their extractors land). Receivers the DDG cannot resolve (call-RHS bindings like x = requests.Session(), parameter receivers, closure captures) and languages without §1c extractors remain at the documented external-exemption fallback by design. SECURITY.md regenerated; ADR-0017 §3a updated in-place to reference the refinement and document residual unresolvable cases. Tests: 31 in test_taint_refine.py (imports, receiver hints, edge rewriter), 1 integration test for cmd_verify_claims plumb-through, 1 helper test for hints_by_caller flow. 100% coverage on the new module in isolation per scripts/check-package-coverage. The narrower 'Option 2 source-line lifting' framing from earlier discussion was rejected in favor of the per-§1c-extractor accretion model the ADR endorses."  # 0a13
